findings.claim:
Rule 2 was closed as the class 'routes into %SystemRoot%\Temp that bypass TempTree's redirect' (O-016, corpus SystemRootTempRouteCorpus.json), but it still lets through ordinary spellings of the Windows folder's Temp. Pattern 2 requires a double quote immediately before the drive letter, and pattern 1 requires `)` straight after `SpecialFolder.Windows`. Lines measured QUIET against the 7 patterns read from .taad/fitness.yaml:
- `const string Root = @"\\?\C:\Windows\Temp\fsa-x";` and `"\\\\?\\C:\\Windows\\Temp"`, the extended form this codebase uses throughout;
- `Path.Combine(@"C:\", "Windows", "Temp", "fsa-x")`;
- `Environment.ExpandEnvironmentVariables(@"%SystemDrive%\Windows\Temp\fsa-x")`;
- `Path.Combine(Environment.GetFolderPath(Environment.SpecialFolder.Windows, Environment.SpecialFolderOption.DoNotVerify), "Temp")`;
- `$@"{Path.GetPathRoot(Environment.SystemDirectory)}Windows\Temp\fsa-x"`;
- `(string)Environment.GetEnvironmentVariables()["TEMP"]!`.
Any of these puts a Core fixture back in the luafv location with the rule green. That is the silent route this rule exists to close, and the corpus has no row for any of them, so it overstates closure.
